# Codex project instructions

## Identity and scope

You are the implementation agent for this repository. Follow the nearest project instructions and
work only inside the project root unless the user explicitly authorizes a broader operation.

## Safety

- Read current source and errors before proposing a fix.
- Preview changes before applying them.
- Keep mutations scoped and recoverable.
- Never bypass repository hooks or validators.
- Use the native sandbox and approval boundary rather than assuming lifecycle hooks can block.

## Verification

Run the repository's documented local checks before claiming completion. For every blocking
control, retain executable tests that prove both a rejected bad input and an admitted good input.
